 "extraction": "VizieR ASU TSV export, -out=**&-out.max=unlimited. Cleaned file maps upstream columns to a standard schema (id,ra_deg,dec_deg,z,z_err,q_flag,member_flag) and appends sep_arcmin and R_proj_Mpc computed from the cluster centre with FlatLambdaCDM(H0=70,Om0=0.3). No rows dropped. Where the upstream redshift is stored as a velocity cz in km/s it is converted to z=cz/c and its uncertainty is converted consistently to dz=e_cz/c; otherwise no values are altered. Raw upstream response kept verbatim in raw/.",
 "note": "Abell 370 (z=0.375). Lagattuta, Richard, Bauer et al. 2019, MNRAS 485, 3738 ('3D structure in the A370 MUSE Mosaic'), table C1 'Master MUSE Redshift Catalog'. 584 redshifts. Quality: column Conf (spectroscopic confidence flag); column Type is a spectroscopic type flag. Instrument: VLT/MUSE mosaic (the earlier, smaller mosaic; largely superseded by the 2022 Pilot-WINGS catalogue above, which contains this data plus more). Selection function: MUSE datacube detection (continuum prior + blind line search), lensing magnification mu is tabulated per object. Sky coverage: to ~1.7 arcmin (~0.55 Mpc projected); 90% within ~0.39 Mpc.",
